{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_page", "label": "Eigene Serializer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avroserializer", "label": "AvroSerializer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nimmt einen kompilierten avsc-Typ entgegen; actor-ts importiert avsc nie selbst, sondern akzeptiert alles mit der passenden Form."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufserializer", "label": "ProtobufSerializer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dekodiert per toObject zu einem einfachen Objekt mit gef\u00fcllten Defaults und 64-Bit-Feldern als Strings, weil ein Journal weder eine Message-Instanz noch ein Long speichern kann; abw\u00e4hlbar mit withPlainObjects(false)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avsc_buffer_trap", "label": "avsc kann kein einfaches Uint8Array dekodieren", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fromBuffer greift auf Buffer-interne Methoden zu, und das Base64-Framing \u00fcbergibt genau ein einfaches Uint8Array \u2014 ein handgeschriebener Avro-Serializer kodiert sauber und scheitert beim Replay, auf Bun, Node und Deno gleicherma\u00dfen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufjs_pooled_bytes", "label": "protobufjs liefert gepoolte Bytes zur\u00fcck", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writer.finish() ist ein Fenster in einen gemeinsamen Schreib-Pool (gemessen ~28 KB Offset in einem 64-KB-Pool auf Node); so gespeichert ist die Zeile eine Sicht auf den Speicher anderer Nachrichten. ProtobufSerializer l\u00f6st sie ab und validiert zus\u00e4tzlich beim Kodieren."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_manifest_guard", "label": "Manifest-Guard gegen fremde Bytes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Avro tr\u00e4gt keine Feld-Tags und Protobuf keinen Nachrichtennamen, fremde Bytes werden also zu plausiblem Unsinn; beide Serializer schreiben ein Manifest und verweigern Payloads, die unter einem anderen geschrieben wurden."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_serializer_id_range", "label": "Serializer-IDs \u2265 100 sind ein Wire-Vertrag", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1-99 geh\u00f6ren den eingebauten (JSON = 1, CBOR = 2), der Konstruktor lehnt Kleineres ab; die ID steckt in jeder gespeicherten Zeile \u2014 \u00e4ndert man sie, h\u00f6ren alte Zeilen auf zu dekodieren."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_compiled_type_not_proto_path", "label": "Ein kompilierter Typ statt eines .proto-Pfads", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": ".proto zur Laufzeit zu laden hie\u00dfe Dateisystemzugriff \u2014 im Browser nicht verf\u00fcgbar, auf Deno berechtigungspflichtig und \u00fcberall eine Sache mehr im Deployment; der kompilierte Typ l\u00e4sst die Wahl zwischen Quell-String, geb\u00fcndeltem Descriptor und generiertem Code, ohne Build-Schritt zu erzwingen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_register_and_bind", "label": "register (ID-Lookup) und bind (Routing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "bind nimmt eine numerische ID, also muss zuerst registriert werden; das Mapping l\u00e4uft \u00fcber den Konstruktor (instanceof), Plain-Objekte fallen auf den Default zur\u00fcck und Subklassen matchen die Bindung des Parents."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_withserializer_store", "label": "withSerializer(...) an einem Persistenz-Store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Weg, auf dem ein eigener Serializer gespeicherte Rows erreicht; die Register<X>Plugins-Bundles verteilen ein geteiltes withSerializer auf alle Stores, der eigene serializer eines Leafs gewinnt. Die In-Memory-Stores ignorieren die Option \u2014 ihr Round-Trip nutzt den strengeren Default-Codec, die sichere Richtung f\u00fcr einen Dev/Test-Default."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_serialized_framing", "label": "__serialized__-Framing { id, manifest, data }", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selbstbeschreibend, damit vor der Konfiguration geschriebene Rows weiter \u00fcber den Default-Codec dekodieren und beide Formate in einem Stream koexistieren; fehlt der Serializer oder hat er eine andere id, wirft decodePayload einen SerializationError, der die ben\u00f6tigte id nennt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_format_per_store_or_per_version", "label": "Ein Format pro Store, oder eines pro Version", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "withSerializer gilt storeweit; wenn v1 als Avro auf der Platte liegt und v2 Protobuf sein soll, verpackt serializerCodec den Serializer und die SchemaRegistry h\u00e4lt ihn pro Version. Jedes Format existiert weiterhin genau einmal, als Serializer."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_handwritten_protobuf", "label": "Handgeschriebenes Protobuf f\u00fcr ein Manifest pro Wert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ProtobufSerializer schreibt ein festes Manifest; muss es aus der Nachricht berechnet werden (etwa ein Versions-Tag), implementiert man das Interface direkt und verifiziert im fromBinary."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_messagepack_example", "label": "MessagePack-Serializer (Beispiel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sitzt zwischen JSON (Gr\u00f6\u00dfe, Parse-Speed) und Protobuf (typisierte Schemas) \u2014 ein CBOR-\u00e4hnliches Format mit breiteren Cross-Language-Libraries."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_stateless_serializers", "label": "Serializer sollten zustandslos sein", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sie k\u00f6nnen von mehreren Actors geteilt, nebenl\u00e4ufig aufgerufen und bei Neustart frisch instanziiert werden."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_when_custom_serializer", "label": "Wann ein eigener Serializer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cross-Language-Interop, schema-erzwungene Evolution mit Schemadateien in der Versionskontrolle, oder spezifische Perf-/Gr\u00f6\u00dfenanforderungen (FlatBuffers f\u00fcr Zero-Copy) \u2014 sonst reichen JSON oder CBOR."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avroserializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_serializer_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufserializer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_serializer_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_messagepack_example", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_serializer_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_withserializer_store", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_serialized_framing", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avsc_buffer_trap", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avroserializer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufjs_pooled_bytes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufserializer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_manifest_guard", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_avroserializer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_manifest_guard", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_migration_schema_registry_serializer_id_mismatch", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_serializer_id_range", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_register_and_bind", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_register_and_bind", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_serializationextension", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_format_per_store_or_per_version", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_migration_schema_registry_per_version_wire_format", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_format_per_store_or_per_version", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_migration_schema_registry_serializercodec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_handwritten_protobuf", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufserializer", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_compiled_type_not_proto_path", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_protobufserializer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/serialization/custom.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_custom_page", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_serialization_overview_registry_not_consulted", "relation": "cites",